<MudPaper Outlined="true" Class="pa-6 pa-md-8 mx-auto" MaxWidth="44rem">
    <MudText Typo="Typo.overline" HtmlTag="p" Color="Color.Primary">Field notes · Issue 14</MudText>
    <MudText Typo="Typo.h4" HtmlTag="h3" GutterBottom="true">What a spring of seeing logs taught us</MudText>
    <MudText Typo="Typo.subtitle1" Class="mud-text-secondary" GutterBottom="true">
        Three months of measurements from the northern dome, and why the coldest nights gave the sharpest images.
    </MudText>
    <MudText Typo="Typo.caption" HtmlTag="p" Class="mud-text-secondary">By Inês Albuquerque · 6 min read</MudText>

    <MudDivider Class="my-5" />

    <MudText Typo="Typo.body1" GutterBottom="true">
        Between March and May the volunteers recorded the seeing every clear hour: how much the atmosphere blurred a
        star at the eyepiece. Ninety-one nights went into the log, and a pattern appeared within the first month.
    </MudText>
    <MudText Typo="Typo.body1" GutterBottom="true">
        Nights that followed a cold front were steadier than warm, still evenings. The difference was large enough to
        change which targets we scheduled first.
    </MudText>

    <MudText Typo="Typo.h6" HtmlTag="h4" Class="mt-6" GutterBottom="true">Cold air, steady air</MudText>
    <MudText Typo="Typo.body1" GutterBottom="true">
        Turbulence comes from layers of air at different temperatures. After a front passes, those layers mix less,
        and the image of a double star stops dancing.
    </MudText>

    <MudText Typo="Typo.h5" HtmlTag="blockquote" Class="my-6 pl-4" Style="border-inline-start: 3px solid var(--mud-palette-primary)">
        “The best night of the season was also the one when nobody wanted to leave the warm room.”
    </MudText>

    <MudPaper Outlined="true" Class="pa-4" Style="background: var(--mud-palette-background-gray)">
        <MudText Typo="Typo.subtitle2" HtmlTag="p">Median seeing by month</MudText>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.body2" HtmlTag="p">March 2.4″ · April 2.1″ · May 1.8″</MudText>
    </MudPaper>
    <MudText Typo="Typo.caption" HtmlTag="p" Class="mud-text-secondary mt-2">
        Table 1. Lower values mean steadier air, in arcseconds, measured at 22:00 local time.
    </MudText>
</MudPaper>
